skellycam research patch for libuvc (https://github.com/libuvc/libuvc) master
@ d07de4fa23905ee8cac06f5d24b2a03d42a3b363 (2026-10-01). Apply with: git apply <this file>
(git apply ignores this preamble). Feature patch only; Windows portability needs no source patch
(see ../compat/win32 and ../CMakeLists.txt).

Part A - per-frame payload-header timing (upstream keeps PTS / last SCR STC internally in
  uvc_stream_handle (pts/hold_pts, last_scr/hold_last_scr) but never copies them into uvc_frame_t,
  ignores the SCR's 11-bit SOF counter ("@todo read the SOF token counter"), and only exposes
  capture_time_finished (CLOCK_MONOTONIC at buffer swap). capture_time (struct timeval) is never set.)
  * uvc_frame_t gains (appended, so the existing prefix layout is unchanged): pts, scr_stc_first,
    scr_sof_first, scr_stc_last, scr_sof_last, has_pts, has_scr, closed_by_eof, fid,
    host_first_payload_ns, host_last_payload_ns, first/last_payload_packet_idx,
    packets_per_transfer, payload_count, error_payload_count.
  * _uvc_stream_callback timestamps each completed transfer (CLOCK_MONOTONIC ns) and the packet
    index; _uvc_process_payload records them for the first/last data payload of each frame.
  * header-only payloads of the previous FID no longer leak timing into the next frame.
Part B - application control of the isochronous alt setting (bandwidth)
  * uvc_stream_set_iso_override(strmh, altsetting, min_bytes_per_packet, packets_per_transfer):
    force a bAlternateSetting (even one smaller than dwMaxPayloadTransferSize), or replace
    dwMaxPayloadTransferSize in libuvc's "first alt that is big enough" search, and/or set the iso
    packets per transfer. uvc_stream_get_iso_info() reports what uvc_stream_start chose.
  * LIBUVC_HAS_SKELLYCAM_PATCH is defined in libuvc.h.

